1
00:00:05,602 --> 00:00:07,343
Beyond cause and effect.

2
00:00:07,423 --> 00:00:11,256
In Dzogchen, few phrases
are so easily misheard.

3
00:00:11,336 --> 00:00:12,927
It sounds like an exception.

4
00:00:13,007 --> 00:00:15,305
A realm where causes stop working.

5
00:00:15,385 --> 00:00:19,127
Or a ground that makes everything,
while nothing makes it.

6
00:00:19,945 --> 00:00:23,914
A careful reader of Madhyamaka
will ask a fair question.

7
00:00:23,994 --> 00:00:27,940
Is this a hidden substance, slipped
back in through a side door?

8
00:00:28,770 --> 00:00:30,633
The answer offered here is no.

9
00:00:30,713 --> 00:00:33,962
The phrase is not an exception
to dependent arising.

10
00:00:34,042 --> 00:00:38,133
It is what dependent arising looks like
once the habit of fixing things has been

11
00:00:38,213 --> 00:00:39,413
seen through.

12
00:00:40,089 --> 00:00:44,085
Most thinking about causes rests
on three quiet assumptions.

13
00:00:44,165 --> 00:00:47,210
That a thing needs an
essence of its own to appear.

14
00:00:47,290 --> 00:00:51,680
That a cause needs a power of
its own, carried into its effect.

15
00:00:51,760 --> 00:00:55,964
And that the meeting of conditions
needs a deeper foundation underneath.

16
00:00:56,773 --> 00:00:59,016
Nāgārjuna looks for each one.

17
00:00:59,096 --> 00:01:03,704
The chariot is not found in its
wheels, its axle or its pole.

18
00:01:03,784 --> 00:01:08,894
The power of a cause, when sought, turns
out to be named only in relation to the

19
00:01:08,974 --> 00:01:11,176
effect it is said to produce.

20
00:01:11,256 --> 00:01:16,041
And the foundation, when sought,
becomes one more thing with parts,

21
00:01:16,121 --> 00:01:18,069
and the parts are named too.

22
00:01:18,881 --> 00:01:21,803
None of this says that
chariots are unreal.

23
00:01:21,883 --> 00:01:25,300
It says that the essence the
search assumed is not there.

24
00:01:26,109 --> 00:01:28,094
Notice what analysis is for.

25
00:01:28,174 --> 00:01:31,368
It is not a mind that must
keep dissecting forever.

26
00:01:31,448 --> 00:01:34,466
It answers one habit, the habit of fixing.

27
00:01:34,546 --> 00:01:38,991
When that habit has been seen through,
there is nothing left to search for.

28
00:01:39,071 --> 00:01:41,074
The dissection ends itself.

29
00:01:41,894 --> 00:01:43,812
But one assumption survives.

30
00:01:43,892 --> 00:01:46,393
It no longer asks what produces things.

31
00:01:46,473 --> 00:01:48,241
It asks why they appear at all.

32
00:01:48,321 --> 00:01:52,716
As if the coming together of
conditions still owed a final reason.

33
00:01:53,525 --> 00:01:57,525
This is the last spell. It is looking
for permission to stop looking.

34
00:01:58,342 --> 00:02:03,140
The question why has force only while
something seems to stand behind appearing.

35
00:02:03,220 --> 00:02:07,963
When nothing is found there, the question
is not answered. It stops applying.

36
00:02:08,043 --> 00:02:11,455
In this book's reading, that
is the sense of the old words,

37
00:02:11,535 --> 00:02:13,403
no why and because.

38
00:02:14,221 --> 00:02:17,700
Two ways of knowing are
at work. One divides.

39
00:02:17,780 --> 00:02:21,233
A cup becomes a handle, a rim and a body.

40
00:02:21,313 --> 00:02:22,972
The other does not divide.

41
00:02:23,052 --> 00:02:27,107
It meets what appears whole, before
the parts and names are added.

42
00:02:27,905 --> 00:02:29,550
These are not two stages.

43
00:02:29,630 --> 00:02:33,178
The dividing mind is the
habit that analysis answers.

44
00:02:33,258 --> 00:02:37,218
The undivided seeing is what
remains when the habit stops.

45
00:02:38,037 --> 00:02:40,688
Then the eight extremes
fall away together.

46
00:02:40,768 --> 00:02:42,535
Arising and ceasing.

47
00:02:42,616 --> 00:02:46,856
Lasting and ending. Coming
and going. Same and different.

48
00:02:46,936 --> 00:02:50,063
All of them needed a thing
with an edge of its own.

49
00:02:50,143 --> 00:02:52,196
Without it, nothing is lost.

50
00:02:52,276 --> 00:02:55,529
Nothing ever had the whereabouts
those questions required.

51
00:02:56,353 --> 00:02:59,778
Dzogchen calls this appearing
spontaneous presence.

52
00:02:59,858 --> 00:03:03,093
It is not a new ingredient
laid over emptiness.

53
00:03:03,173 --> 00:03:06,341
Dependent arising describes
it from the outside.

54
00:03:06,421 --> 00:03:10,865
Spontaneous presence describes
the same appearing from within.

55
00:03:10,945 --> 00:03:15,299
Emptiness itself is empty,
so it cannot become a ground.

56
00:03:16,122 --> 00:03:19,072
The old teaching to
Bāhiya names the taste.

57
00:03:19,152 --> 00:03:21,287
In the seen, only the seen.

58
00:03:21,367 --> 00:03:23,488
In the heard, only the heard.

59
00:03:23,568 --> 00:03:28,556
No seer stands behind the seeing.
Colours are vivid. Sounds are immediate.

60
00:03:28,636 --> 00:03:30,816
Thoughts lose their heavy ownership.

61
00:03:31,630 --> 00:03:33,629
This is not an attainment to keep.

62
00:03:33,709 --> 00:03:36,949
The moment it is held,
the fixing has returned.

63
00:03:37,765 --> 00:03:40,579
Seen is just seen. Heard is just heard.

64
00:03:40,659 --> 00:03:43,015
And nothing needs to be put in its place.

